CELLS = [
    ['md', "## 1. Geom types and the dispatch table\n`collision_driver.py::MJ_COLLISION_TABLE` maps every ordered type pair `(t1 <= t2)` to PRIMITIVE, CONVEX or nothing. Example 16.1 prints it from the library's own dicts, plus `MJ_FLEX_COLLISION_TABLE` and the one cell `DisableBit.NATIVECCD` flips (box-box)."],
    ['example', 'ex1_collision_table.py', '16.1'],
    ['md', '## 2-4. Pair order, the Geom struct and the launches\n`_add_geom_pair` stores the lower geom type first, so `contact.frame[0]` points from the lower type to the higher. The primitive path is **one** `wp.launch(_primitive_narrowphase(...), dim=d.naconmax)` whose static if-chain holds only the pair types with `m.geom_pair_type_count > 0`; the convex path launches one kernel per present convex pair type (a grid-stride loop for non-heightfield pairs; heightfield pairs get one thread per pool slot). Example 16.8 records the launches by wrapping `wp.launch` (module hashes can differ on your machine; on GPU the convex `dim` is a few device waves).'],
    ['example', 'ex8_type_pair_launches.py', '16.8'],
    ['md', '## 5. `write_contact`: detected, active, margin and gap\nDetected: `dist < margin + gap` (strict, float32). Active: `dist < margin`, or in the gap band with adhesion (then condim 1). Note the boundary row at exactly `margin + gap`.'],
    ['example', 'ex6_margin_gap.py', '16.6'],
    ['md', '## 6. Material mixing\n`contact_material_params`: explicit pair first, then priority (in 4.0.1 a direct, negative solref on either geom still gives the element-wise min), else max condim, element-wise max friction, solmix-weighted solref/solimp and summed adhesion; friction is clamped to `mjMINMU`.'],
    ['example', 'ex5_material_mixing.py', '16.5'],
    ['md', '## 7. Primitive colliders\n### 7.1 Plane-sphere\n`dist = (c - p)·n - r`, `pos = c - n (r + dist/2)`: the midpoint between the surfaces.'],
    ['example', 'ex2_plane_sphere.py', '16.2'],
    ['code', '# Interactive geometry: plane_sphere and capsule-capsule closest points, the same formulas as the page widgets.\n%matplotlib inline\nimport numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n\ndef plane_sphere(tilt_deg=10, cx=0.05, cz=0.12, r=0.08):\n    th = np.radians(tilt_deg)\n    n = np.array([-np.sin(th), np.cos(th)])          # plane normal through the origin\n    c = np.array([cx, cz])\n    dist = c @ n - r                                  # collision_primitive_core.plane_sphere\n    pos = c - n * (r + 0.5 * dist)\n    t = np.array([n[1], -n[0]])\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(6, 3))\n    ax.plot(*np.array([-t * 0.5, t * 0.5]).T, lw=3, label="plane")\n    ax.add_patch(plt.Circle(c, r, alpha=0.3))\n    ax.plot(*pos, "o", color="C3", label=f"contact.pos, dist = {dist:.4f}")\n    ax.arrow(*pos, *(n * 0.06), width=0.003, color="C3")\n    ax.set_aspect("equal"); ax.set_xlim(-0.4, 0.4); ax.set_ylim(-0.1, 0.3); ax.legend(loc="upper left")\n    plt.show()\n\ntry:\n    from ipywidgets import interact\n    interact(plane_sphere, tilt_deg=(-30, 30, 1), cx=(-0.3, 0.3, 0.005), cz=(-0.02, 0.27, 0.005), r=(0.03, 0.12, 0.005))\nexcept ImportError:\n    plane_sphere()\n'],
    ['md', '### 7.3 Capsule-capsule\n`_segment_weights` returns two closest-point pairs only for parallel segments (relative test `|ab x cd|^2 <= 1e-8 |ab|^2 |cd|^2`).'],
    ['example', 'ex3_capsule_capsule.py', '16.3'],
    ['md', 'Sweep: one world per yaw angle of the rod; only parallel (to within the 1e-8 test, about 0.006 deg) gives 2 contacts.'],
    ['code', '# Sweep the rod\'s yaw over one world per angle and count capsule-capsule contacts per world.\nSWEEP = """\n<mujoco><worldbody>\n  <geom type="capsule" fromto="-0.3 0 0.5  0.3 0 0.5" size="0.05"/>\n  <body pos="0 0 0.59"><freejoint/><geom type="capsule" fromto="-0.2 0 0  0.2 0 0" size="0.05"/></body>\n</worldbody></mujoco>"""\nyaw = np.linspace(0.0, 90.0, 91 if ON_GPU else 31)\nmjm_s = mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_string(SWEEP)\nm_s = mjw.put_model(mjm_s)\nd_s = mjw.make_data(mjm_s, nworld=len(yaw), nconmax=4, njmax=16)\nq = np.tile(mjm_s.qpos0, (len(yaw), 1))\nq[:, 3], q[:, 6] = np.cos(np.radians(yaw) / 2), np.sin(np.radians(yaw) / 2)\nd_s.qpos.assign(q.astype(np.float32))\nmjw.kinematics(m_s, d_s)\nmjw.collision(m_s, d_s)\nn = min(int(d_s.nacon.numpy()[0]), d_s.naconmax)\ncount = np.bincount(d_s.contact.worldid.numpy()[:n], minlength=len(yaw))\nprint(f"contacts at yaw {yaw[:3].round(1).tolist()} deg:", count[:3], "| worlds with 2 contacts:", int((count == 2).sum()))\ntry:\n    import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n    fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(7, 2.8))\n    ax.step(yaw, count, where="mid")\n    ax.set_xlabel("yaw of the rod [deg]"); ax.set_ylabel("contacts"); ax.set_yticks([0, 1, 2])\n    ax.set_title("capsule-capsule: 2 contacts only when parallel")\n    plt.show()\nexcept ImportError:\n    print("skipped: matplotlib not installed")\n'],
    ['md', '### 7.5 Plane-box\nAll 8 corners go to `write_contact` with `id_ = i`; only those within margin + gap survive. The corner index becomes `contact.geomcollisionid`.'],
    ['example', 'ex4_plane_box.py', '16.4'],
    ['md', '## 8. Box-box: separating axes and clipping\nDefault box-box is CONVEX (GJK/EPA + a max-area quad, 4 contacts). With NATIVECCD disabled, `box_box` (SAT over 15 axes + face clipping) keeps up to 8 clipped vertices, like MuJoCo C.'],
    ['example', 'ex7_box_box_native.py', '16.7'],
    ['md', '## 9. Surface velocity: conveyor belts\n`<geom surfacevel=...>` is a batched field; `_contact_surfacevel` projects it on the contact frame and `_add_surface_vel` adds it to the friction rows. One belt speed per world. Both kernels run only if `m.flg_surfacevel` is True, which `put_model` copies from the MJCF: per-world values on a model whose XML has no nonzero surfacevel are silently ignored (set `m.flg_surfacevel = True` in that case).'],
    ['example', 'ex9_conveyor.py', '16.9'],
    ['md', "## 10. Calling a core collider from your own kernel (private API)\nThe timing line is your device's number; on a CPU it is a CPU number, never a GPU number."],
    ['example', 'ex10_core_kernel.py', '16.10'],
    ['md', '## 11. Checking against MuJoCo C\nMatch contacts by geom pair and position, never by pool index.'],
    ['example', 'ex11_vs_mujoco_c.py', '16.11'],
    ['md', '## Exercise 16.1: your own plane_capsule\nFill in the kernel: each end sphere of the capsule is a `plane_sphere`. The asserts compare with the contacts MJWarp wrote.'],
    ['code', 'import mujoco\nimport numpy as np\nimport warp as wp\nwp.config.log_level = wp.LOG_WARNING\nimport mujoco_warp as mjw\n\nTILTED_ROD = """\n<mujoco><worldbody>\n  <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="5 5 .1"/>\n  <body name="rod" pos="0 0 0.3"><freejoint/>\n    <geom name="rod" type="capsule" size="0.05 0.2" margin="1"/></body>\n</worldbody></mujoco>"""\nNWORLD = 6\n\n@wp.kernel\ndef my_plane_capsule(geom_xpos: wp.array2d(dtype=wp.vec3), geom_xmat: wp.array2d(dtype=wp.mat33),\n                     radius: float, half: float, dist_out: wp.array2d(dtype=float)):\n    w = wp.tid()\n    # TODO: plane normal = z-axis of geom 0; capsule axis = z-axis of geom 1\n    # TODO: dist_out[w, 0] and dist_out[w, 1] for the two end spheres\n\nmjm = mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_string(TILTED_ROD)\nm = mjw.put_model(mjm)\nd = mjw.make_data(mjm, nworld=NWORLD, nconmax=4, njmax=16)\nrng = np.random.default_rng(3)\nq = np.tile(mjm.qpos0, (NWORLD, 1))\nq[:, 2] = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.4, NWORLD)\nquat = rng.normal(size=(NWORLD, 4)); q[:, 3:7] = quat / np.linalg.norm(quat, axis=1, keepdims=True)\nd.qpos.assign(q.astype(np.float32))\nmjw.kinematics(m, d)\nmjw.collision(m, d)\n\nmine = wp.zeros((NWORLD, 2), dtype=float)\nwp.launch(my_plane_capsule, dim=NWORLD, inputs=[d.geom_xpos, d.geom_xmat, 0.05, 0.2], outputs=[mine])\nn = min(int(d.nacon.numpy()[0]), d.naconmax)\nwid, dist = d.contact.worldid.numpy()[:n], d.contact.dist.numpy()[:n]\nfor w in range(NWORLD):\n    theirs = np.sort(dist[wid == w])\n    assert len(theirs) == 2, theirs\n    assert np.allclose(np.sort(mine.numpy()[w]), theirs, atol=1e-5), (mine.numpy()[w], theirs)\nprint("my plane_capsule matches MJWarp in all", NWORLD, "worlds")'],
    ['solution', 'import mujoco\nimport numpy as np\nimport warp as wp\nwp.config.log_level = wp.LOG_WARNING\nimport mujoco_warp as mjw\n\nTILTED_ROD = """\n<mujoco><worldbody>\n  <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="5 5 .1"/>\n  <body name="rod" pos="0 0 0.3"><freejoint/>\n    <geom name="rod" type="capsule" size="0.05 0.2" margin="1"/></body>\n</worldbody></mujoco>"""\nNWORLD = 6\n\n@wp.kernel\ndef my_plane_capsule(geom_xpos: wp.array2d(dtype=wp.vec3), geom_xmat: wp.array2d(dtype=wp.mat33),\n                     radius: float, half: float, dist_out: wp.array2d(dtype=float)):\n    w = wp.tid()\n    p = geom_xpos[w, 0]\n    n = wp.vec3(geom_xmat[w, 0][0, 2], geom_xmat[w, 0][1, 2], geom_xmat[w, 0][2, 2])  # plane z-axis\n    c = geom_xpos[w, 1]\n    R = geom_xmat[w, 1]\n    axis = wp.vec3(R[0, 2], R[1, 2], R[2, 2])                    # capsule axis = its local z\n    dist_out[w, 0] = wp.dot(c + axis * half - p, n) - radius    # end sphere +axis\n    dist_out[w, 1] = wp.dot(c - axis * half - p, n) - radius    # end sphere -axis\n\nmjm = mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_string(TILTED_ROD)\nm = mjw.put_model(mjm)\nd = mjw.make_data(mjm, nworld=NWORLD, nconmax=4, njmax=16)\nrng = np.random.default_rng(3)\nq = np.tile(mjm.qpos0, (NWORLD, 1))\nq[:, 2] = rng.uniform(0.1, 0.4, NWORLD)\nquat = rng.normal(size=(NWORLD, 4)); q[:, 3:7] = quat / np.linalg.norm(quat, axis=1, keepdims=True)\nd.qpos.assign(q.astype(np.float32))\nmjw.kinematics(m, d)\nmjw.collision(m, d)\n\nmine = wp.zeros((NWORLD, 2), dtype=float)\nwp.launch(my_plane_capsule, dim=NWORLD, inputs=[d.geom_xpos, d.geom_xmat, 0.05, 0.2], outputs=[mine])\n\nn = min(int(d.nacon.numpy()[0]), d.naconmax)\nwid, dist = d.contact.worldid.numpy()[:n], d.contact.dist.numpy()[:n]\nfor w in range(NWORLD):\n    theirs = np.sort(dist[wid == w])\n    assert len(theirs) == 2, theirs\n    assert np.allclose(np.sort(mine.numpy()[w]), theirs, atol=1e-5), (mine.numpy()[w], theirs)\nprint("my plane_capsule matches MJWarp in all", NWORLD, "worlds")\n', 'Exercise 16.1'],
    ['md', '## Exercise 16.2: predict the mixed friction\nFill in `predicted` with the 5-vector `contact.friction` for the floor against each ball. MJCF `friction="0.2"` sets only the first entry.'],
    ['code', 'import mujoco\nimport numpy as np\nimport warp as wp\nwp.config.log_level = wp.LOG_WARNING\nimport mujoco_warp as mjw\n\nPAIRS = """\n<mujoco><worldbody>\n  <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="5 5 .1" friction="0.8 0.01 0.001"/>\n  <body pos="0 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g1" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.3"/></body>\n  <body pos=".5 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g2" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="1.2 0.002 0.002"/></body>\n  <body pos="1 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g3" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.2" priority="2"/></body>\n  <body pos="1.5 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g4" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.9 0.05" solmix="10"/></body>\n  <body pos="2 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g5" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.4 0 0" priority="1"/></body>\n</worldbody></mujoco>"""\n\npredicted = {"g1": [...], "g2": [...], "g3": [...], "g4": [...], "g5": [...]}   # your answers\n\nmjm = mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_string(PAIRS)\nm = mjw.put_model(mjm)\nd = mjw.make_data(mjm, nworld=1, nconmax=8, njmax=32)\nmjw.kinematics(m, d)\nmjw.collision(m, d)\nn = min(int(d.nacon.numpy()[0]), d.naconmax)\nfor g, fr in zip(d.contact.geom.numpy()[:n], d.contact.friction.numpy()[:n]):\n    nm = mujoco.mj_id2name(mjm, mujoco.mjtObj.mjOBJ_GEOM, int(g[1]))\n    assert np.allclose(fr, predicted[nm], rtol=1e-5, atol=1e-7), (nm, fr)\nprint("all 5 friction predictions correct")'],
    ['solution', 'import mujoco\nimport numpy as np\nimport warp as wp\nwp.config.log_level = wp.LOG_WARNING\nimport mujoco_warp as mjw\n\nPAIRS = """\n<mujoco><worldbody>\n  <geom name="floor" type="plane" size="5 5 .1" friction="0.8 0.01 0.001"/>\n  <body pos="0 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g1" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.3"/></body>\n  <body pos=".5 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g2" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="1.2 0.002 0.002"/></body>\n  <body pos="1 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g3" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.2" priority="2"/></body>\n  <body pos="1.5 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g4" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.9 0.05" solmix="10"/></body>\n  <body pos="2 0 .099"><freejoint/><geom name="g5" type="sphere" size=".1" friction="0.4 0 0" priority="1"/></body>\n</worldbody></mujoco>"""\n\n# your prediction: the 5-vector contact.friction for floor + g1 .. g5\npredicted = {\n    "g1": [0.8, 0.8, 0.01, 0.001, 0.001],      # equal priority: element-wise max\n    "g2": [1.2, 1.2, 0.01, 0.002, 0.002],      # max per element, mixes sources\n    "g3": [0.2, 0.2, 0.005, 0.0001, 0.0001],   # priority 2 wins: g3\'s own (defaults)\n    "g4": [0.9, 0.9, 0.05, 0.001, 0.001],      # solmix does not affect friction\n    "g5": [0.4, 0.4, 1e-5, 1e-5, 1e-5],       # priority wins, zeros clamp to mjMINMU\n}\n\nmjm = mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_string(PAIRS)\nm = mjw.put_model(mjm)\nd = mjw.make_data(mjm, nworld=1, nconmax=8, njmax=32)\nmjw.kinematics(m, d)\nmjw.collision(m, d)\nn = min(int(d.nacon.numpy()[0]), d.naconmax)\nfor g, fr in zip(d.contact.geom.numpy()[:n], d.contact.friction.numpy()[:n]):\n    nm = mujoco.mj_id2name(mjm, mujoco.mjtObj.mjOBJ_GEOM, int(g[1]))\n    assert np.allclose(fr, predicted[nm], rtol=1e-5, atol=1e-7), (nm, fr)\nprint("all 5 friction predictions correct")\n', 'Exercise 16.2'],
    ['md', '## Stretch: implement sphere_box\nTransform the sphere centre into the box frame, clamp to the half-extents, handle the centre-inside case with the nearest face, and compare `dist` and the normal with MJWarp for 16 random poses.'],
    ['code', '# your sphere_box here\n'],
    ['solution', 'import mujoco\nimport numpy as np\nimport warp as wp\nwp.config.log_level = wp.LOG_WARNING\nimport mujoco_warp as mjw\n\nSPHERE_BOX = """\n<mujoco><worldbody>\n  <body name="box" pos="0 0 0"><freejoint/><geom name="box" type="box" size=".2 .1 .05" margin="1"/></body>\n  <body name="ball" pos="0 0 .3"><freejoint/><geom name="ball" type="sphere" size=".08"/></body>\n</worldbody></mujoco>"""\n\ndef my_sphere_box(c, r, bpos, bmat, half):\n    local = bmat.T @ (c - bpos)                       # sphere centre in the box frame\n    clamped = np.clip(local, -half, half)             # closest point of the box\n    v = clamped - local\n    L = np.linalg.norm(v)\n    if L < 1e-15:                                     # centre inside the box: nearest face\n        face = np.argmin(half - np.abs(local))\n        nrm = np.zeros(3); nrm[face] = -np.sign(local[face])\n        return -(half[face] - abs(local[face])) - r, bmat @ nrm\n    return L - r, bmat @ (v / L)                      # normal points sphere -> box\n\nNW = 16\nmjm = mujoco.MjModel.from_xml_string(SPHERE_BOX)\nm = mjw.put_model(mjm)\nd = mjw.make_data(mjm, nworld=NW, nconmax=4, njmax=16)\nrng = np.random.default_rng(0)\nq = np.tile(mjm.qpos0, (NW, 1))\nquat = rng.normal(size=(NW, 4)); q[:, 3:7] = quat / np.linalg.norm(quat, axis=1, keepdims=True)\nq[:, 7:10] = rng.uniform(-0.3, 0.3, (NW, 3))\nd.qpos.assign(q.astype(np.float32))\nmjw.kinematics(m, d); mjw.collision(m, d)\nn = min(int(d.nacon.numpy()[0]), d.naconmax)\nwid = d.contact.worldid.numpy()[:n]; dist = d.contact.dist.numpy()[:n]; nrm = d.contact.frame.numpy()[:n, 0]\nxp, xm = d.geom_xpos.numpy(), d.geom_xmat.numpy()\nfor i in range(n):\n    w = wid[i]\n    dd, nn = my_sphere_box(xp[w, 1], 0.08, xp[w, 0], xm[w, 0], np.array([.2, .1, .05]))\n    assert abs(dd - dist[i]) < 1e-5 and np.allclose(nn, nrm[i], atol=1e-4), (w, dd, dist[i], nn, nrm[i])\nprint("sphere_box matches on", n, "contacts")\n', 'Stretch'],
]
